architecture site-fragment-migration
  canonical_name SiteFragmentMigration
  family surface
  domain Surface / Authored fragment migration
  layer surface
  semantic_question How can compiled source literals become reviewable draft fragments without claiming publication or replacing an exact SurfaceIR slot?
  purpose Clang literal candidates carry source byte identity into a reviewed page/slot/audience map. The native planner emits draft coordinates and explicit review records; CMS admits only unseen draft coordinates in one transaction, while a rebuildable semantic index proposes reuse without becoming the exact address or an authority source.
  maturity implemented
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurface/tools/ast_literal_candidates.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurface/tools/plan_fragment_migration.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurface/tools/stage_fragment_migration.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurface/tools/build_fragment_semantic_index.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/site_fragment.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurface/tests/fragment_migration_native.test.mjs
  witness cmd/BonfyreSurface/tests/fragment_migration_native.test.mjs proves literal source identity, human text extraction, review isolation, duplicate-equivalence counts, atomic draft-only CMS import, skip-existing behavior, and a separate rebuildable index manifest
  consumes SourceArtifact
  publishes DerivedView
  internal_calculus Clang AST ranges and source bytes name candidates; an authored function map decides exact page, slot and audience; the native planner assigns draft-only coordinates and leaves unreviewed functions unadmitted. The staging tool applies the CMS schema and imports all new drafts in one transaction. A read-only CMS scan produces a distinct semantic-index generation in a fresh work directory; no index result is written back into canonical content.
  invariant a candidate without a reviewed page/slot/audience mapping stays in review and never enters CMS
  invariant stage is create-only and draft-only; existing coordinates are not overwritten, and publication requires a separate exact SurfaceIR and carrier witness
  invariant semantic similarity may propose reuse but cannot satisfy exact coordinate equality or grant effect authority
  invariant work and vector outputs use fresh generation paths and are never deleted by the index builder
  forbidden_inference a Clang string literal or approximate semantic neighbour -> authored, published, or still-desired user-facing copy

interaction fragment-migration-proposes-surface-copy
  source site-fragment-migration
  destination surface-ir
  relation proposes-draft-coordinate
  preserves source digest, authored page/slot/audience map, draft state and exact coordinate
  drops the assumption that a compiled fallback may be removed at admission time
  forbidden_inference a draft coordinate -> a published surface or authority to remove its compiled fallback
